        <p>ANSWERS TO CORRESPONDENTS. F. WRIGHT, Warrington :—Since the publication of the Problem which you sent 0 us as originul ltkt week, our attention has been drawn to the fact that it is not original. Tnis position first appeared about last July in " Hobbies," winning first prize in tile 'Stroke "Problem Competition. then,i . has also appeared in the t7.september issue of the "Scottish Draughts Quarterly," the "Leeds Mercury Weekly Supplement," and several other papers. The author of ti.e position when it ori2ineiy appeared in " Hobbies " was Thomas Duncan, Perth. We should feel much obliged if you would kindly forward Us an explanation of this, as it is int our intention or desire, t 3 publish anything in this column which is erroneous. J. LEE, Warrington :—Many thanks for problem; as you will notice by the Solvers' List, we have awarded vou two points for the solution of Prob- lem No. 17 along with the other solvers. The points for Problem 18 will only be awarded nest week. Kindly forward your full address with your next solution. SOLUTION OF PROBLEII No. 18. *BY NIR. F. WRIGHT. WARRINGTON. 12— 8 6-13 11-15 28-19 19-23 10— 6 • 4-11 (-21 14 - 9 1-19 15-24 White Wins. *See Answers to Correspondents.</p>
