      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-02-03_WidnesExaminer_art0024" n="art0024">
        <head>PRESENTATIONS TO WARRINGTON. DRUIDS.</head>
        <p>PRESENTATIONS TO WARRINGTON. DRUIDS.</p>
        <p>On Saturday afternoon a public meeting was held in Wash-lane schollroom. Councillor W. Pierpoint, -J.P., presided over a fair attendance of members and friends. The presentation of £3O was made to Brother James Gee ( who had been afflicted with blindness) by the Grand Treasurer, and Grand Becretary of the Order of Druids Friendly Society. The money had been grantA t.O Brother Gee, who 'belongs to the Latchford Lodge of the Warrington Equalized District Branch, by the Board of Manage- Ment of the Order, and the recipient will receive In addition hi 4 ordinary sick benefits. Votes of thanks were afterwards passed to the Chairman for his kindness in being present, and to the Vicar for the use of the schoolroom.</p>
