      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-02-03_WidnesExaminer_art0035" n="art0035">
        <head>OUR LOCAL CHURCHES.</head>
        <p>OUR LOCAL CHURCHES.</p>
        <p>ADDRE33 AT TEE CEIBISTADELPRIAN ROOM. Mr. &amp;lathy, of Stockpert, io speaking on the above suti .ct on Sunday in the Christadelphian Room, Bold. street, introduced the same by sayiug. that ssorne would think it unnecessary one out of place to ask who should preach the gospel, as their opinion was that no one but an ordained priest of Rome or England ought to do so. Before preaching the gospel it was necessary the preacher sheuld know it, and the spiritual guides of to-day know not the gospel, for they taught that under certain con- ditions we should go to heaven at death, which was not in the Bible at all. Touching on the point that "No prophecy of the scripture is of any private interpreta- tion," the lecturer poieted out that though" Eye bath not seen nor ear heard, neither have entered into the heart of man the things which God bath prepared for them that love Hun, yet what was very often omitted was the fact evert sated, that" Ged bath revealed them unto us .by His Spirit." God had given them a t 3,t whereby they might kncw when he had spoken, and the lecturer applie i thistest to several events, both past and current, proving how God ha l re- vealed things by His Spirit in the word. "The meek shall inherit the earth "were the words 9f Jesus Christ and the Psalmist, a state of things the very opposite of that which was now the position of the meek, but one which they had positive assurance would be the lot of those whom Christ approved wueu c to the earth. The Apostle Peter's irquectlon. was "If any man speak, let him speak as the oracles of God," and Paul, speaking of the preaching hf the Goipel, said " Thoueh we or an angel from heaven preach any other gospel unto yota than that which we have preached tilt? you, let him be accursed." If the first test were applied to the things taught in the churches and chapels of tc-lay,they would find that the curse et Paul was upon the preachers of to. day,for they did not speak in accordance w!th the Bible but preached another goliel.</p>
