      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-02-03_WidnesExaminer_art0048" n="art0048">
        <head>RUNCORN AND WIDNES.</head>
        <p>RUNCORN AND WIDNES.</p>
        <p>THE DEPARTURE OF I:JPERINTENTDENT °SELL.</p>
        <p>Mtn the busiueFs of the Rtinc irn Petty 8-!ssions, on Monday, was concluded, the chairman (Mr. Joseph Handley), congratulated SuparintendeLt Okell, and wished him good luck, health and prosperity, in his new coarters within the salubrious neighbourhood of Altrinc- ham rn behalf of the Bench, the Clerk and the other officers of the Court, for thlugh sorry to pal with him, they heartily congratilated him—Mr. J. Ashton also spoke eulogising Mr. Okell.—Mr. Okell thanked them n all for their kind remarks.</p>
