        <p>DISPENSARY BALL.</p>
        <p>VISIT OP THE LORD CakNOELLOR</p>
        <p>The annual ball of this charitable institution was held on Tuesday evening at the Lion Hotel, Bridge- street. The attengance as usual included the elite of the town an I district. Mr. E G. Davies (h3n. secretary to the Ball Committee), in a circular issued to those ladies and gentleman usually at- tending the ball, said :—" Up war Is of 5,000 poor persons receive medicine and advice at this institu- tion annutlly. Many of these are labourers, who are employe' in the agricultural dii-tricts of L Inca- shire and Cheshire, but have to find their homes, and ail in timi of sickness, at Warrington. As the expenses of the charity are heavy and increasing, donations in aid of the Ball Fund are solicited, mil will be gratefully received by the lion3rary secret- tary."The handsome ball room of the hotel had been artistically decorated by Mr. Ralph Johnson, and the guests were enabled to move about amid sur- roundings of the ple.asantest. Among those pre- sent were the L ird Chancellor of England and C mn- tess Halsbury, and Lady E. Glifford. Dancing commenced at 9 p.m. and WAS continued until 2 a.m., the music by Mr. Pearson's orchestra being excellent. There were 20 dances on the programme. Mrs. Gilbert, the manageress of the hotel, supplie the refreshments, and succeeded in appeasing the wants of all in a satisfactory manner. Toe following is a list of the Baal Committee and stewards :—The Mayor of Warrington (Alderman Wright). Captain C. S. dridge (The King's) an Messrs. John White, Henry Greenill, C. Harold Broadbent, J. S. Sherratt, It. E. Wynn -Jones, Her- bert Ridgway, A. J. Edelsten, F. W. Monks, F. M. Appleton, J. D. Fairclough, J. D. Buckten' and E. G Davies (hon. secretary), to whom much praise is due fn. their exertions to make the ball a success About 183 ladies and gentlemen were present,which is an increase upon the number in attendance at the previous ball. The following is a list of those present : Warn. Major Johnson, Missil Broadbent, Mrs Kin4don, Mr G ii K Broadbent, Mr T Ifsernp, Lady Beatrice Brosdbent. Miss hi Kemp, Mr Broadbent. Miss Sylvia Litton. Mi G Banninz, Maiir GreAves Litton, Miss J Btrnabv, Mr ii H Leadbetter, Dr Best. Mr W Laadbetter, Mrs Burrows, Dr L tuder, Mr Bower. Dr -- Lyon, Mrs</p>
