        <head>LORD NEWTON'S WILL</head>
        <p>LORD NEWTON'S WILL</p>
        <p>The exemotor of the will, dated February 16th, 1880, of Wilfilm John, first Baron Newton, of Lyme Hall, Disley, S.olknort, and 20, BAgrave-square, formerly from 1859 to 1885 M.P. for South Lancashire, and from 1868 to 1885 M. P. for East Cheshire, who died on Deaerolor 15:h last, aged seventy ye tr 3, is the testator's son, Maj r and the Hon. Gilbert Legh, to whom is devisei all of the real estate and the•residuary personal estate. Pi)wer is reserved tergrant p-obate also to the testator's widow, Emily Jane, Liidy Newton (daughter of the Van, r ttil I Charles Wodehouse, Archdeacon of Norwich), and to her Lord Newton t.eqileaths £l,OOO Under pewers of August Ist and December 18:h. 1867, the cnpyhold estate is charged with £20,000 in favour of his younger children. The tetator bequeaths to his two daughters Du!cibella Jane and Mabel Maud such sums as will make up the portion of each daughter to £25,909.</p>
