        <p>PLnkSI-NT SATURDIY EVANING.</p>
        <p>The entertainment on Stturd ty evening in the C )-3perative II ill was given by the memb Ins of the Primitive m. t iodist Cnriscian End;avour S wiety. The gathering was presided over by M. C. T. Rawlings. Tnere wis a very fair au hence Sing were given by Mr. Rawlings, Misses Woods, L. Stronach, Tohnahs, M. Slronalh, Messrs. Wehster and Sims, recitations by Misses Nedie Dickens MA. Ward.n, and Mr J T Austin, dialogues by Masters C Rawlin ;I and F B auconjustru nentalists: Vi )lin, Mr. G Mat Rids ; harp, Muss Woods Miss Toombs; organ, Mrs Rawlingc.</p>
        <p>Sr. JOHN'S WIWI= WORiECILS SOCUL GATE RUING.</p>
        <p>The members of the ciaoir and °fibers of itiohn's Church, an 1 tne teachers of the Sunday school were entertained to tea by the Vicar, the Rev. T. It. Aattiews, in the iNfission Hall on Wednesday even- ing. Abut 6) persons were present to tea and the repast was t oroughly enjoyed. The subsequent proceedings were of a musical char actpr, an ex lent program ne of songs being submitted, AI% Elarriaon, organist p:.esiding at the plan). It ifre ih- mmt3 were handed round about 9-30, the annual cake presented by &amp;Ir. Niolyneux being distributed.</p>
