        <p>Oo Mond ty evening, In olmts G+rri:v, wno resides at 34. Liverporq-street, Sc. Helens, fell in tha street at War- rington and a clb pi.gead over him. • Ho was immedi- ately conveyed to the Infirmary where his injuries.which were not serious consisting of bruises and a scalp wound, were attended to.</p>
        <p>.--....p.......... WARRINGTON RARKETS.</p>
        <p>At the Warrington Cora Market on Wednesday, new whew, (white) fetched 4s (701 b t) the bushel); red wheat, 3i 101 to 34 lid; new oats, 2s 21 to 24 51. Flour, best seconds, per 2401b4, 194 31 to 20s. Bean, 11/1 to is 31 per 201 b. Prices in the Warrington Provision Market were' :—Fresh batter, 1s 2d and la 41 per lb; he'll eggs, 8 and 9 for is; fowls, 44 61 to 58 per couple; ducks, 5s to 6s English beef, 5d to 10o; mutton, 61 to 91; veal, 6d to l 01; pork, 61 to Bd.</p>
