      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-02-03_WidnesExaminer_art0135" n="art0135">
        <head>BRICK-STREET MISSION BAND OF HOPE.</head>
        <p>BRICK-STREET MISSION BAND OF HOPE.</p>
        <p>On Tuesday evening the fourth entertain-nent was given in the schoolroom under the presidency of Mr. James Shaw. There was a very good attend- ance. The Chairman, in his address, speaking as a life-long abstainer urged those present to adopt the principle of total abstinence, and forcibly depicted th sad and ruinous effects of strong drink by strik- ing arguments and narratives which have come under his own observation, pressing home at the same time the happy results of being firm and steadfast in times of temptation. The following recited :—Ellen Clarke, Bessie Shaw, Elizabeth Gallop, Letty Warburton, Fred Brown, and Thomas Wright,. The juvenile choir rendered a chorus entitled " Temperanci Bells." and solos were sung very sweetly by Cissy Holt," Where is my wander- ing boy to-night " ; Bessie Shaw, "Remember me, Oh Mighty One " ; and Elizabeth Gallop, " Have courage my boy to say No." The following dialogues were creditably rendered, viz, "The Teetotal Alphabet," "Almost Ruined," and "Two Christmas Visitors." The entertainment, which proved to be very profitable and enjoyable, con- I cluclod with the singing of the Doxology.</p>
