      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-02-03_WidnesExaminer_art0138" n="art0138">
        <head>BRITISH WOMEN'S TEMPERANCE ASSOCIATION.</head>
        <p>BRITISH WOMEN'S TEMPERANCE ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>The Warrington branch of the British Women's Temperance Association have recently held two gospel temperance meeting., the first one at Elles- mere-street, when Mrs. H. Roberts took the chair, and Mrs. R. Garnett was the speaker. Other ladies present as helpers were—Mrs. and Miss Isaac, Miss Shaw Green, Mrs. Reed, and Miss E. Bennett. The latter gave a recitation. On Monday, a second meeting was held in the Girls' Clubroom, Silver- street, when Miss Bessie Dutton gave an address to the girls. Miss Emily Bennett was asked to preside and Mrs. Davies. Miss Ashdown, and Miss G. Shaw Green nig) took part in the meeting. A large num- ber of pledges were taken on each occasion.</p>
