        <p>or of many "good things," may be the beginning of chronic indigestion: but indigestion just as often comes wAnift any apparent cause. A heavy, loaded feeling on the stomach after meals; an *empty, vacant ache before food; sallownes of the skin; frequent bilious attack.; sluggish liver; spots before the eyes, and especially GETTING NO BENEFIT FROM FOOD TAKEN, all spring from indigestion or chronic dyspepsia. Gastric ulcer may follow, with unspeakable agonies—perhaps in the ma Cancer of the Stomach—if you neglect these symptoms. They have been cured in time many times by Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale fteopie.</p>
        <p>good health ever since taking Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People, and if I feel the least symptom of my old complaint, I take a Pill or two and am all right again. I always keep some in tlif house, in case of need." The latter is a proper precaution, as. while Dr. Wil- liams' Pick Pills are unlike any other medicine, and their effects are permanent, no other medicine has as much usefulness, as a atrenthening and tonic medicine, for men and women. NEARLY DEAD FROM GASTRIC ULCER. --- CLERGYMAN SUMMONED TO THE BEDSIDE. --- CURE BY DR. WILLIAMS' PINK PILLS. --- THE CURE CERTIFIED AT Sr. GEORGE'S HOSPITA L. At 23, Ceylon-road, Hammersmith, London, W., re- sides Mr. James Vincent, from whom a representative of the West London Advertiser heard a wonderful story. Mr. Vincent proved to be a hale, hearty man—a matter for surprise when it is known that recently his life was despaired of by the doctor in attendance, hi., mother was telegraphed for, and a clergyman's services were hastily requisitioned. Asked what were the symptoms of his illness, Mr. Vincent, who is twenty- nine years of age, said : "I was at my work as a porter when I was taken ill and sent to Charing Cross Hospital. They found that I was suffering hem gastric ulcer. Abut two next morning I brought up a great clot of blood. My wife did not think I should live long, and the dolor was evidently of the same opinion, for he allowed her to get a clergyman to see me. She tele- graphed for my mother. I had wasted to a shadow, although before I was taken ill I weighed 13 stone. I could not digest anything ; I could not even keep mi;k on my stomach. It was Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People that pulled me up as lam now. The first two pills I took relieved me. I saw an announcement in a newspaper where a man who had been suffering like me bad been cured by Dr. Williams' Pink Pills. I may tell von that I had lost a pint and a half of blood. These pills have certainly done me a worts] of good. I have taken seven boxes- I went to St. George's Hospital a few weeks ago. They sounded me, sad told me there was no ulcer there now. though, of course, they form' there had been one. I believe it was work that pulled me down. I had such a nasty vain also, that I did not know what to do. I have never bad that pain since I started taking Dr. Willame' Pink Pills.</p>
